  "causal_conclusion": "Original input release clears and LGC/ATCA commands automatic braking. The 0.2-second rate sample is an early transient. Holding maximum proportional-rate input until the held gyro integral reaches the angle produces approximately 12-degree / 35-degree terminal yaw overshoot. The current harness stop rule, rather than absent braking, prevents settled-angle fidelity.",
